Z||000000||2xsess||10-27-2000||11:05 PM||||My headlight motor seems to have destroyed it's gear. I looked at Rodneys site, I thought someone was making brass gears for the 84-86 headlights. <P>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodney||10-28-2000||07:22 AM||||Alan Mooty makes the brass gears although I have not heard of anyone buying any in some time. He gets $40 per gear. For just a little more you can get all new OEM pieces WITH the brush/contact assemblies. Rebuilt they should last another 100,000 miles. All on my web page. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-28-2000||02:08 PM||||Rodney carries good stuff even if he's guilty of a shameless plug  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I used his repair kit for my 87 light motors.<P>You can rebuild them or replace the whole system. If you do a good job the rebuilt will last years. <P><BR>If you don't have the patience or skill for that sort of thing then an upgrade to the gen2 system is likely better for you. It's not hard, just a little time consuming. I've been told the same system used on 87&up Fiero is on some other GM cars, like the sunbird with the little flap doors. (I have been looking but haven't seen one yet. I just want it for spare parts.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||10-28-2000||09:25 PM||||Rodney, even though you posted a shameless plug, I'll be ordering a kit from your site either tomorrow or Monday.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||14
